<title>USA: Cornell Corrections Q4 net profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Cornell Corrections Q4 net profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Actual		  Pro Forma</p>
<p>		  Three months ended   Year Ended	Year Ended</p>
<p>		    December 31,     December 31,    December 31,</p>
<p>			     1996    1995     1996    1995     1996</p>
<p> Revenues		$10,381 $5,280  $32,327 $20,692  $42,061</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	 571  (873)  (2,379)   (989)    1,772</p>
<p>Earnings (loss) per share</p>
<p>				 .08  (.22)    (.53)   (.25)	.25</p>
<p>Number of shares used to</p>
<p>  compute EPS	    6,987  3,983    4,466   3,983    7,200</p>
<p>			  (000's except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Cornell Corrections Inc pro forma results assume the acquisitions of the Big Spring Correctional Center and the Reid Center had occurred at the beginning of the respective periods, assume the initial public offering had occurred at the beginning of the respective periods and exclude non-recurring charges recognized in the third quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>Net loss for fiscal 1996 included non-recurring charges of $870,000 of noncash general and administrative compensation expense and a $1.3 million charge to interest expense for the early retirement of indebtedness.</p>
</text>
